1
00:00:01,431 --> 00:00:03,691
In this video, we're going to talk about

2
00:00:03,691 --> 00:00:05,782
the first two steps of reprocessing:

3
00:00:05,782 --> 00:00:08,194
the bedside pre-clean and the leak test.

4
00:00:08,869 --> 00:00:11,297
Both are quick, and both are the steps

5
00:00:11,297 --> 00:00:12,819
most often cut short.

6
00:00:13,533 --> 00:00:15,528
By the end, you'll know what a proper

7
00:00:15,528 --> 00:00:17,895
bedside clean involves, you'll see how a

8
00:00:17,895 --> 00:00:20,191
leak test protects the scope, and you'll

9
00:00:20,191 --> 00:00:22,066
understand why neither can ever be

10
00:00:22,066 --> 00:00:22,735
skipped.

11
00:00:25,865 --> 00:00:28,229
Reprocessing starts in the procedure room,

12
00:00:28,269 --> 00:00:30,913
done by the busiest person, at the busiest

13
00:00:30,913 --> 00:00:34,168
moment. That's exactly why it's the step

14
00:00:34,168 --> 00:00:35,799
most often abbreviated!

15
00:00:38,665 --> 00:00:40,889
The pre-clean happens immediately after

16
00:00:40,889 --> 00:00:43,040
the procedure, before the scope leaves the

17
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:45,979
room. Wipe the insertion tube.

18
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:48,819
Then suction or flush the channels with

19
00:00:48,819 --> 00:00:50,281
the agreed solution.

20
00:00:53,365 --> 00:00:56,820
Why the rush? Because organic material,

21
00:00:56,825 --> 00:00:59,685
like blood and mucus, starts to dry inside

22
00:00:59,685 --> 00:01:03,411
the channels. Bacteria settle into it, and

23
00:01:03,411 --> 00:01:05,695
within minutes they begin forming biofilm,

24
00:01:05,695 --> 00:01:07,858
a protective matrix stuck to the channel

25
00:01:07,858 --> 00:01:11,416
wall. Once it has formed, no later step

26
00:01:11,416 --> 00:01:12,890
reliably removes it.

27
00:01:16,031 --> 00:01:18,815
Next, the leak test, before immersion,

28
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:21,195
every time, without exception.

29
00:01:21,834 --> 00:01:24,142
Following the manufacturer's method, the

30
00:01:24,142 --> 00:01:26,294
scope is pressurised with air through its

31
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:28,873
connector, so fluid can't get in.

32
00:01:29,539 --> 00:01:31,854
If the sheath or a channel is breached,

33
00:01:31,895 --> 00:01:34,238
the pressure reading falls, or, with the

34
00:01:34,238 --> 00:01:36,967
pressurised scope in clean water, a stream

35
00:01:36,967 --> 00:01:39,030
of bubbles shows exactly where.

36
00:01:42,131 --> 00:01:44,182
Here's what happens when it's skipped!

37
00:01:44,845 --> 00:01:47,321
A damaged scope is immersed, and fluid

38
00:01:47,321 --> 00:01:49,845
gets into its interior, where it can't be

39
00:01:49,845 --> 00:01:51,464
cleaned or disinfected.

40
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:54,870
Organisms multiply inside, and the scope

41
00:01:54,870 --> 00:01:57,105
keeps going to patients until the damage

42
00:01:57,105 --> 00:01:58,603
is found some other way.

43
00:01:59,269 --> 00:02:01,600
Tested properly, the damaged scope is

44
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,844
caught and taken out of use first.

45
00:02:06,965 --> 00:02:08,415
Time for a knowledge check.

46
00:02:09,103 --> 00:02:11,026
Why is the leak test performed before

47
00:02:11,026 --> 00:02:14,194
immersion, every time, without exception?

48
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:16,586
Pause here and think it through.

49
00:02:23,865 --> 00:02:26,197
Because a scope with a breach admits fluid

50
00:02:26,197 --> 00:02:28,152
into its interior when immersed.

51
00:02:28,815 --> 00:02:30,690
That interior can't be cleaned or

52
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:33,815
disinfected, so organisms multiply there,

53
00:02:33,815 --> 00:02:36,383
and the scope is irreparably contaminated,

54
00:02:36,471 --> 00:02:38,642
while still being used on patients.

55
00:02:39,344 --> 00:02:41,483
The test takes about a minute, and it's

56
00:02:41,483 --> 00:02:43,294
skipped when the list runs late.

57
00:02:46,398 --> 00:02:49,701
Let's recap! Pre-clean at the bedside,

58
00:02:49,701 --> 00:02:52,550
immediately, before organic material dries

59
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:53,976
and biofilm forms.

60
00:02:54,653 --> 00:02:57,225
Leak test before every immersion, without

61
00:02:57,225 --> 00:03:00,591
exception. And remember, one skipped

62
00:03:00,591 --> 00:03:02,887
minute can contaminate a scope for every

63
00:03:02,887 --> 00:03:06,480
patient after. Next, we'll look at manual

64
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:08,772
cleaning and high-level disinfection.

